<pre><code>if (x &lt; 0) {
    new IllegalArgumentException("x must be nonnegative");
}
</code></pre>
<p>It was probably the intent of the programmer to throw the created exception:</p>
<pre><code>if (x &lt; 0) {
    throw new IllegalArgumentException("x must be nonnegative");
}
</code></pre>

